# cww services env — copy to ~/.cww/services.env if you need it. Mode 600.
#
# Everything in this file is loaded verbatim into EVERY workspace container
# (compose env_file), read at 'cww create' time — the pass-through for env
# your app or its tooling needs at runtime. It is machine-wide: prefer
# per-project 'environment:' entries in the repo's
# .cww/docker-compose.services.yml when a value belongs to one project.
#
# Agent credentials do NOT belong here — they live in ~/.cww/env, and each
# workspace receives only the key of the auth method it was created with.
# Git credentials live in ~/.cww/credentials (see examples/cww.env.example).
#
# Examples:
# NPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY=https://registry.example.internal
# SENTRY_DSN=...
